        "summary": "Lionel predicts Tyler Robinson will not live to face trial, describes a hypothetical in-custody death narrative, compares the situation to his belief about Jeffrey Epstein’s death, discusses Candace Owens and Erika Kirk, and challenges whether the rifle has been forensically connected to Charlie Kirk’s killing.",
        "description": "A monologue built around predictions and allegations rather than a report of a new death. Lionel imagines how officials and media might respond if Tyler Robinson were found dead in custody, alleges Epstein was murdered despite the official suicide determination, proposes unusually controlled protective custody, and disputes the evidentiary connection between a recovered rifle and the killing. All such assertions remain attributed commentary.",
